<title>USA: EntreMed thalidomid tests expanded.</title>
<headline>EntreMed thalidomid tests expanded.</headline>
<dateline>ROCKVILLE, Md. 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>EntreMed Inc said Tuesday an expansion of the number of brain cancer patients currently under observation in the National Cancer Institute- sponsored Phase II clinical trials using thalidomide treatment.</p>
<p>The collaborative clinical trials agreement, established in 1995 between the two organizations and Bristol-Myers Squibb Co, was designed to study the anticancer effects of thalidomide in breast, prostate and brain cancer as well as Kaposi's sarcoma.</p>
</text>
